    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3860": {
      "title": "Advancement and Alumni Affairs Office – Senior Officer/ Officer",
      "description": "Advancement and Alumni Affairs Office – Senior Officer/ Officer About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 7,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures young talent with critical thinking, innovative minds, caring attitudes, moral values and social responsibility. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education, top-quality faculty members, award-winning green campus facilities, innovative degree programmes, a unique residential college system that combines living and learning, interactive small-class teaching, close student-teacher relationships, impactful research, and excellent student development and support services. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Advancement and Alumni Affairs Office – Senior Officer/ Officer (Ref: SO/O (AAAO) 2026-08-28) Responsibilities organise and provide marketing and logistics support for fundraising campaigns; liaise with internal and external stakeholders on fundraising-related affairs; arrange and coordinate campus visits, receptions and ceremonies; prepare write-ups, presentations and reports for fundraising projects; provide administrative and secretarial support for work committee(s); develop and compile regular communications with stakeholders through office’s website, social media platforms and e-news; manage and update the donor database ; and provide administrative support to the Office. Applicants Should possess a recognised bachelor’s degree, with at least 5 years of post-qualification hands-on work experience, preferably in higher education; have a strong command of written and spoken English and Chinese; good understanding of database management and digital marketing tools would be an advantage; strong interpersonal and communication skills; and self-motivated, well-organised, able to work with minimum supervision and under tight timeline. .................................................................................................................................................................. Applicants with less experience will be considered for the post of Officer. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 13 September 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3857": {
      "title": "Graduate School",
      "description": "Graduate School - Senior Executive Officer About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 7,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures young talent with critical thinking, innovative minds, caring attitudes, moral values and social responsibility. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education, top-quality faculty members, award-winning green campus facilities, innovative degree programmes, a unique residential college system that combines living and learning, interactive small-class teaching, close student-teacher relationships, impactful research, and excellent student development and support services. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place in China. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among China’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Graduate School - Senior Executive Officer (Ref: SEO (GS) 2026-08-21) Responsibilities collaborate with stakeholders , admission team and programme offices to manage the end-to-end admission process f or postgraduate programmes, from application review, vetting to issuing offers, ensuring efficien cy , quality, and compliance with university policies and deadlines; act as the primary point of contact for prospective students by addressing inquiries and offering guidance on the application process; leverage data analytics to track admission metrics, identify trends, and generate reports to support decision-making and process improvement; represent the Graduate School at various recruitment events, information sessions; collaborate with relevant parties to develop and enhance the Postgraduate Admission System ; and assist with the Secretariat work of Graduate Studies Committee . Applicants Should possess a bachelor’s degree with a minimum of 5 years of relevant work experience; have previous experience in handling admissions-related matters and in workflow automation; have relevant administrative experience, along with competence in committee work, will be an advantage; possess proficiency in data analysis and report generation, knowledge of IT applications will be a definite advantage; have good command of written and verbal English and Chinese (including Putonghua); have effective administrative abilities and strong organisational, coordination and problem-solving skills; and demonstrate a strong sense of accountability and attention to detail. .................................................................................................................................................................. The appointee is expected to assume duty in September 2026 . Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 6 September 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3856": {
      "title": "Graduate School",
      "description": "Graduate School - Executive Officer About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 7,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures young talent with critical thinking, innovative minds, caring attitudes, moral values and social responsibility. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education, top-quality faculty members, award-winning green campus facilities, innovative degree programmes, a unique residential college system that combines living and learning, interactive small-class teaching, close student-teacher relationships, impactful research, and excellent student development and support services. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place in China. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among China’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Graduate School - Executive Officer (Ref: EO (GS) 2026-08-21) Responsibilities support the end-to-end admission process for postgraduate programmes, from application review, vetting to issuing offers, ensuring efficien cy , quality, and compliance with university policies and deadlines; act as the primary point of contact for prospective students by addressing inquiries and offering guidance on the application process; support postgraduate scholarship administration; manage websites, and assist in the compilation of reports and statistics; support the s ecretariat work of Graduate Studies Committee ; and represent the Graduate School at various recruitment events, information sessions . Applicants Should possess a bachelor’s degree with a minimum of 3 years of relevant work experience; previous experience in handling admissions-related matters; have good command of written and verbal English and Chinese (including Putonghua); have effective administrative abilities and strong organisational, coordination and problem-solving skills; proficiency in data analysis and report generation, knowledge of IT applications will be a definite advantage; demonstrate a strong sense of accountability and attention to detail; and relevant administrative experience, along with competence in committee work, will be an advantage. .................................................................................................................................................................. The appointee is expected to assume duty in September 2026.  Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 6 September 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3855": {
      "title": "Graduate School - Assistant Officer",
      "description": "Graduate School - Assistant Officer About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 7,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures young talent with critical thinking, innovative minds, caring attitudes, moral values and social responsibility. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education, top-quality faculty members, award-winning green campus facilities, innovative degree programmes, a unique residential college system that combines living and learning, interactive small-class teaching, close student-teacher relationships, impactful research, and excellent student development and support services. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Graduate School - Assistant Officer (Ref: AO (GS) 2026-08-21) Responsibilities provide administrative and clerical support to the Graduate School; coordinate and organise various events and activities hosted by the Graduate School; handle student inquiries and maintain communication with postgraduate students through various communication channels ; handle purchases, reimbursements, payments, and other financial and budgeting matters for various reporting purposes; manage and maintain the Graduate School’s website, promotional materials, surveys and reports, ensuring its accuracy and relevance; and offer assistance to other units within the Graduate School as needed. Applicants Should possess a recognised bachelor’s degree with at least 1 year of experience in tertiary institutions; have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese ( Cantonese and Putonghua ) ; possess strong computer literacy, including proficiency in Chinese word processing; have good communication and interpersonal skills; and be a team player and have the ability to quickly learn and adapt. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 6 September 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3853": {
      "title": "Department of Marketing - Executive Officer / Assistant Officer",
      "description": "Department of Marketing - Executive Officer / Assistant Officer About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 7,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures young talent with critical thinking, innovative minds, caring attitudes, moral values and social responsibility. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education, top-quality faculty members, award-winning green campus facilities, innovative degree programmes, a unique residential college system that combines living and learning, interactive small-class teaching, close student-teacher relationships, impactful research, and excellent student development and support services. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. Department of Marketing - Executive Officer / Assistant Officer (Ref: EO/AO (MKT) 2026-08-21) Responsibilities provide support for academic staff to perform teaching and administrative duties; assist in the planning and implementation of initiatives on mentorship, internship and overseas exchange, etc.; create and curate content on websites and social media platforms; organise activities to engage students, alumni, and external stakeholders; and liaise with external stakeholders, such as educational institutions, business enterprises, trade associations, nonprofit organisations, and government agencies, to advance the Department’s strategic goals. Applicants Should possess a bachelor’s degree with at least 3 years of relevant work experience, preferably in the tertiary education sector; have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua); have proficiency in the use of office software applications and good knowledge of social media platforms; have good organisational and communication skills and the ability to work independently; and be a team player, accountable and proactive. Applicants with less experience will be considered as an Assistant Officer. .................................................................................................................................................................. S alary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicants should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 6 September 2026 .  Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only.  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3859": {
      "title": "School of Decision Sciences",
      "description": "School of Decision Sciences - Executive Officer About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 7,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures young talent with critical thinking, innovative minds, caring attitudes, moral values and social responsibility. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education, top-quality faculty members, award-winning green campus facilities, innovative degree programmes, a unique residential college system that combines living and learning, interactive small-class teaching, close student-teacher relationships, impactful research, and excellent student development and support services. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : School of Decision Sciences - Executive Officer (Ref: EO (SDSC) 2026-08-28) Responsibilities planning, developing and implementing marketing and promotional strategies for the School and its undergraduate and postgraduate programmes; coordinating integrated promotional campaigns across online and offline channels, including social media, recruitment events, information seminars, exhibitions and other outreach activities; developing and managing promotional content for the School’s website, newsletters, social media platforms and other communication channels; liaise with internal and external stakeholders to execute school-related activities and events; provide administrative support to the development and operation of academic programmes offered by the School; provide secretariat support to committees and workgroup; and supporting the day-to-day administration of the School. Applicants Should hold a recognised bachelor’s degree, preferably in marketing, communications, public relations, business administration or a related discipline, with at least 3 years of relevant work experience; have hands-on experience in branding and marketing, corporate communications, public relations, digital content development or event promotion within the tertiary education sector; be proficient in Microsoft Office 365 applications, have knowledge of graphic design and multimedia tools, ability to use content management systems and analytics tools; have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, including Cantonese and Putonghua; demonstrate strong organisational, project management and stakeholder engagement skills; be creative, detail-minded, self-motivated and capable of managing multiple assignments independently while working effectively as part of a team; and possess excellent interpersonal and communication skills. M arketing experience, website content management, and use of digital marketing, social media analytics tools will be an advantage. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 13 September 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3854": {
      "title": "Research Assistant – Department of Supply Chan and Information Management",
      "description": "Research Assistant – Department of Supply Chan and Information Management About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 7,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures young talent with critical thinking, innovative minds, caring attitudes, moral values and social responsibility. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education, top-quality faculty members, award-winning green campus facilities, innovative degree programmes, a unique residential college system that combines living and learning, interactive small-class teaching, close student-teacher relationships, impactful research, and excellent student development and support services. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites application for the Research Project “ Mass Customizing Artificial Intelligence-Based Inspection Systems ”, funded by the Research Matching Grant Scheme: Research Assistant – Department of Supply Chan and Information Management (Ref: RA (SCM – RMGS#840009) 2026-08-21) Responsibilities The appointee will work with faculty members to apply deep learning and natural language processing in business-related research topics. Applicants Should have a recognised bachelor’s degree or above in Computer Science and Engineering, Electronic Engineering, or a related discipline; preferably possess experience in natural language processing and deep learning ; be proficient in Python; be familiar with tensorflow or pytorch; possess strong programming skills; and be a responsible person and willing to learn. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 6 September 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
